NNECTICUT IS BLANK FROM 2022. The returns are published for the eight legacy counties, while the boundaries from 2022 onward are the nine planning regions under new GEOIDs. The two do not nest, so joining them would need a crosswalk that does not exist here.","Small gaps by design: ballots belonging to no county (Connecticut statewide write-in, Maine UOCAVA, Rhode Island federal precinct) and Kansas City, which Missouri reports separately from the four counties it spans, are dropped rather than misattributed. Nationally this is about 3,400 votes in 2020 plus Kansas City’s 136,645.","Years before 2010 are drawn on 2010 county boundaries, the oldest vintage this project ships. County lines barely moved over that span, but Broomfield County, Colorado was created in 2001 and has no returns for 2000."]}}